  "help.gettingStarted": "Getting started",
  "help.gettingStartedDesc": "A 3-minute tour of how this console actually works.",
  "help.quickStart": "Quick start (5 steps)",
  "help.step1.title": "Pick (or create) a workspace",
  "help.step1.body":
    "Click <Hop>Issues</Hop> in the sidebar to enter the issue view. If you do not have a workspace yet, create one first under <Hop>Workspaces</Hop> and bind it to your repo.",
  "help.step1.cta": "Open issue view",
  "help.step2.title": "Create a new issue",
  "help.step2.body":
    'In the workspace console, type at the bottom what you want done (e.g. <em>"Add a /api/ping endpoint that returns &#123;pong: true&#125;"</em>) and press <Kbd>↵</Kbd>. The system spins up a per-issue git worktree on a new branch automatically.',
  "inbox.firstRunTitle": "First time here? Three steps.",
  "inbox.firstRunDesc":
    "No issues yet. Run through the quickstart and you'll have an agent writing real code in under 5 minutes.",
  "inbox.firstRun.step1":
    "Use Issues in the sidebar to enter the issue view. If you do not have a workspace yet, create one first under Workspaces and bind it to your repo.",
  "inbox.firstRun.step2":
    "In the workspace console, type what you want done at the bottom and press Enter.",
  "inbox.firstRun.step3":
    "Open the issue → DAG tab → Auto-plan or pick a template → Save graph → Start. Watch the agents work.",
  "inbox.firstRun.openIssues": "Open Issues →",
  "inbox.firstRun.readGuide": "Read the full guide",
  "help.step3.title": "Plan the work",
  "help.step3.body":
    "Open the issue → <Hop>DAG</Hop> tab. Two ways:<br />• <b>Auto-plan</b> — let the orchestrator LLM propose a graph<br />• <b>Pick a template</b> — Feature / Bug fix / Hotfix / Refactor / Docs<br />Then click <b>Save graph</b> → <b>Start</b>.",
  "help.step4.title": "Watch the agents",
  "help.step4.body":
    'PM → Architect → Engineer → QA dispatch in sequence. Each tile shows live status (e.g. <em>"Engineer: Working… Editing api.py"</em>).<br />• <b>alt-click</b> any tile → "Why did the agent decide this?" drawer<br />• <b>Steer</b> button (top right) → drop a mid-run hint<br />• <b>Fork</b> button → branch off to try a different direction',
  "help.step5.title": "Ship it",
  "help.step5.body":
    "Issue header status flips to <b>Done</b> when QA passes. Open <Hop>Diff · Merge</Hop>:<br />• <b>Open GitHub PR</b> → push branch + open a real PR via <code>gh</code><br />• <b>Squash-merge</b> → merge locally if you skip the PR loop<br />• <b>Take over locally</b> → copy <code>cd path && code .</code> to your clipboard if you want to grab the worktree manually",
  "help.pageMap": "Page map",
  "help.insideIssue": "Inside an issue",
  "help.keyboardShortcuts": "Keyboard shortcuts",
  "help.concepts": "Concepts in 30 seconds",
  "help.backToInbox": "Back to Inbox",
  "help.feat.dag": "DAG",
  "help.feat.dag.body":
    "The 5-character canvas (Conductor + PM/Architect/Engineer/QA). Live status, alt-click for explain drawer, Auto-plan + 5 templates if no graph yet.",
  "help.feat.tasks": "Tasks · Runs",
  "help.feat.tasks.body":
    "Task list (one per role) + the most recent run's logs/messages/result. Switch CHAT / REFINE / RERUN modes for follow-ups.",
  "help.feat.artifacts": "Artifacts",
  "help.feat.artifacts.body":
    "Persisted files for this issue: PRD, system design, implementation report, QA report. Refresh button + auto-poll while a phase is in flight.",
  "help.feat.diff": "Diff · Merge",
  "help.feat.diff.body":
    "git diff vs base branch + Submit / Open GitHub PR / Squash-merge / Abandon (with 60s undo).",
  "help.feat.steer": "Steer",
  "help.feat.steer.body":
    "Mid-run hint to the next agent dispatch. Lands in `_steer.md` on disk and auto-injects into prompts.",
  "help.feat.fork": "Fork",
  "help.feat.fork.body":
    "Branch the issue's current state into a sibling issue — try a different direction without losing the original.",
  "help.feat.undo": "Abandon undo",
  "help.feat.undo.body": "Abandon shows a 60-second countdown bar; click Undo to restore.",
  "help.shortcut.cmdK": "Jump to issue / workspace / page (command palette)",
  "help.shortcut.altClick": "On a DAG node — open the agent reasoning drawer",
  "help.shortcut.upDown": "In command palette — move selection",
  "help.shortcut.enter": "In command palette — open the highlighted result",
  "help.shortcut.esc": "Close any palette / dialog / drawer",
  "help.concept.project": "Project",
  "help.concept.project.body":
    "A git repo registered with the console. Workspaces and issues live inside.",
  "help.concept.workspace": "Workspace",
  "help.concept.workspace.body":
    "A session within a project. Holds many issues; mostly cosmetic grouping.",
  "help.concept.issue": "Issue",
  "help.concept.issue.body":
    "One unit of work. Owns its own git branch <code>issue/&lt;id&gt;-&lt;slug&gt;</code> and a worktree on disk.",
  "help.concept.dag": "DAG",
  "help.concept.dag.body":
    "The planned sequence of agent dispatches. Nodes are roles, edges are sequence/refine-loop/parallel.",
  "help.concept.task": "Task",
  "help.concept.task.body":
    "One agent invocation against an issue. Owns its own prompt, status, result, run history.",
  "help.concept.run": "Run",
  "help.concept.run.body":
    "One shell-out to the CLI (codex / claude). A task can have multiple runs (rerun/refine/chat).",
  "help.concept.artifact": "Artifact",
  "help.concept.artifact.body":
    "The structured output a role persists to <code>issues/&lt;id&gt;/&lt;role&gt;/</code>: PRD, design, implementation report, QA report.",
  "help.concept.steer": "Steer note",
  "help.concept.steer.body":
    "Mid-flight user hint stored at <code>issues/&lt;id&gt;/_steer.md</code>; injected into the next agent's prompt as authoritative.",
  "help.concept.memory": "Team memory",
  "help.concept.memory.body":
    "<code>.agent-collab/team_notes.md</code> at the project root. Issue completions append a summary; once it's accumulated past 5 entries the orchestrator LLM distills evergreen lessons.",
  "help.page.inbox.desc": "Cross-project KPIs, status distribution, recent issues.",
  "help.page.workspaces.desc": "CRUD workspaces; click a workspace to open its console.",
  "help.page.approvals.desc":
    "Issues / task reviews / agent questions / Codex tool calls awaiting your decision.",
  "help.page.artifacts.desc":
    "Cross-issue browser of every PRD / design / engineer report / QA report.",
